A-4 Keyboard / A-5 Visible focus — PASS.
  The trigger is a real element, not a click handler on a bare <th>:
    buttonTags = [BUTTON:button, BUTTON:button, BUTTON:button, BUTTON:button]
    tabIndex = 0 (natural tab order)
  Real key presses through the browser, not synthetic events:
    focus the "File" button, press Enter  -> aria-sort becomes "ascending"
    press Space                            -> aria-sort becomes "descending"
  Focus indicator on the focused button while :focus-visible matches (true):
    box-shadow: rgb(99,102,241) 0 0 0 2px   (indigo-500 ring, 2px)
    outline: solid rgba(0,0,0,0) 2px        (Tailwind focus:outline-none is a
                                             transparent outline, not removal)
  Ring contrast vs its adjacent background, computed from the actual colors:
    light thead bg rgb(249,250,251): 4.26:1 ; dark thead bg ~rgb(24,32,48): 3.95:1
  Both exceed the 3:1 A-5 threshold, so "never outline:none without an
  equal-or-better replacement" is satisfied.

A-7 Real table semantics — PASS. It is still a <table>; all five header cells
  carry scope="col" (thScope = [col,col,col,col,col]), and the swap responses
  contain scope="col" x5 as well, so semantics survive the swap.

A-9 Never color-only — PASS. renderIndicators() (filemanager.html:517-539)
  sets th.setAttribute('aria-sort', 'ascending'|'descending') on the active
